column17:
There is no officially recognized energy poverty rate at the municipal or national level in Turkey. However, according to recent sources:
Approximately 5-7% of the population is estimated to live in energy poverty (Climate Scorecard, 2025
).
An earlier academic assessment based on 2017 Household Budget Survey data suggests that around 25% of households are energy poor—and nearly half of the lowest-income households are at risk (Turan, E. & Keskin, G. (2019), Energy Poverty in Turkey, ResearchGate
).
This issue is currently being further studied within the framework of İzmir's SECAP (Sustainable Energy and Climate Action Plan) update process.
